During the RADIAL trial, a total of 169 tickets were submitted to the RADIAL helpdesk across 29 of the 38 participating sites. Ten sites did not enroll participants, but three of them still submitted tickets, indicating that approximately 90% (n = 26) of sites with participants engaged with the support system at least once. An internal identifier was designated for tickets raised by clinical operations or the support team not attributed to a single site. This category accounted for 16% (n = 27) of all submissions. As shown in Fig. 6, ticket submissions peaked between February 2024 and September 2024, coinciding with the period of highest number of participants actively enrolled in the trial. Ticket distribution per country, along with corresponding participant numbers and ticket-to-participant ratios, is summarized in Table 3.Fig. 6
